From: mscharged-port
Subject: Native LLP64 widths for operator new sizes and pointer cache keys
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; apply after 0644.

64-bit Windows is LLP64: unsigned long stays 32-bit while size_t and pointers
are 64-bit. 63 class-local operator new overloads spelled their size parameter
unsigned long, which is the size type on the Wii and on LP64 hosts; natively
they now take __SIZE_TYPE__ (identical on Linux and macOS). The bounding-box
cache in DrawableModel/RenderShadow is keyed by a model's address; natively the
key is __UINTPTR_TYPE__ instead of unsigned long. Console spellings remain
behind the MSCHARGED_NATIVE conditionals.

